---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HowToSchema from '../../components/seo/HowToSchema.astro';

const today = '2026-07-03T00:00:00+00:00';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator is a free, privacy-first browser tool that compares real monthly hosting costs across 8 cloud providers: Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare, AWS Amplify, Supabase, Firebase, Render, and Railway. Enter your expected bandwidth, requests, CPU hours, storage, and auth users to see exactly what each provider will charge you. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator factors in every free tier, credit, and gotcha so you only see what you actually pay. Everything runs instantly in your browser. No signup, no server, no data collection.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does it cost to host a web app at 10,000 users?',
    a: 'It depends entirely on what kind of app. A lightweight SaaS dashboard at 10K monthly users typically runs $50–150/month across most stacks. The same user count on an image-heavy or media app can hit $300–800 because of bandwidth costs. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator asks you what kind of app you\'re building first. That\'s the variable that matters most, more than the user count itself.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What\'s the cheapest stack for a Next.js SaaS?',
    a: 'For most Next.js SaaS apps under 50K users, the cheapest credible stack is Cloudflare Pages + Workers paired with Supabase or a VPS-hosted Postgres. Cloudflare doesn\'t charge for bandwidth, which is the cost line that bites most growing apps. Run your specific numbers through the Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator. For some app types Vercel + Supabase can be competitive once you factor in developer time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is my hosting bill so much higher than the pricing page suggested?',
    a: 'Three usual suspects. First, bandwidth: most pricing pages quote a generous-looking included amount, but image-heavy or media apps blow past it fast, and overage rates are $0.09–$0.15 per GB. Second, compute meters you didn\'t notice: active CPU time, function invocations, image optimization, and edge requests are often billed separately from the base plan. Third, per-seat charges if your team grew. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator surfaces all three so you can see which one is going to hit you.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are there any fixed-price platforms for hosting?',
    a: 'Mostly no. The industry standard is base fee plus usage-based overages, which is why surprise bills happen. Closest you\'ll get to fixed pricing: a VPS (Hetzner, DigitalOcean, Contabo) at $5–20/month flat, where you self-host. Render\'s plan tiers are the most predictable among managed PaaS options. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator flags which providers in your comparison have hard spending caps available. That\'s the closest thing to safety.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much will my hosting cost at 100,000 users?',
    a: 'At 100K users the spread between providers gets wide. Typically $200 to $2,000+/month depending on stack and app type. This is the point where bandwidth-free platforms (Cloudflare, Railway) pull significantly ahead of bandwidth-charging ones (Vercel, Netlify, Amplify) for image- or media-heavy apps. Use the Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator\'s grid view to see the full spread before you commit to a stack.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What\'s the cheapest backend for a static site?',
    a: 'If your site is genuinely static (no logins, no database), you don\'t need a backend. Cloudflare Pages or GitHub Pages will host it free indefinitely. If you need light dynamic features (form submissions, comments, simple auth), Cloudflare Workers + D1 or Supabase free tier are the cheapest credible options. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator\'s "no backend needed" toggle covers this case.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Vercel vs Cloudflare vs Netlify, what\'s the actual cost difference?',
    a: 'At identical usage, the gap can be 5–10× for bandwidth-heavy apps. Cloudflare doesn\'t charge for bandwidth at all. Vercel charges $0.15/GB after 1TB and meters CPU, memory, and invocations separately. Netlify uses a credit system that bundles bandwidth, compute, and deploys into one allowance. Easy to mis-estimate. Run your specific app type and user count through the Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator to see the real numbers.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are the hidden costs of cloud hosting?',
    a: 'The four most-missed line items, in rough order of damage caused: (1) egress bandwidth: every GB leaving the provider is metered; (2) database operations: read amplification from listeners or unindexed queries scales fast; (3) per-seat team charges that compound with team size; (4) build minutes and deploy credits that drain even when your app has no traffic. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator includes all four in its estimates.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I run my SaaS for under $5/month?',
    a: 'At pre-launch or early validation stage, yes. Generous free tiers across Cloudflare Pages, Supabase, and Firebase will keep you at $0. Once you have real users (a few hundred MAU), $5/month becomes harder on managed platforms; a $5 Hetzner or DigitalOcean VPS with self-hosted Postgres is the standard way to stay under that line. The tradeoff is your time managing the server.',
  },
  {
    q: 'When should I move from a managed PaaS to a VPS?',
    a: 'Two common trigger points. First, when you\'re running 4+ small projects on managed services. Each project\'s base fee compounds and a single $20 VPS can host them all. Second, when your managed database bill alone passes $200–300/month. That\'s usually when self-hosted Postgres on a VPS starts paying off, factoring in the time cost of managing it yourself. Below those thresholds, managed services almost always win on total cost (including your time).',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does my hosting provider not tell you about pricing?',
    a: 'A few common omissions: pricing pages quote the base plan but rarely the overage rates in the same view; "free tier" almost never means "capped": it means "soft limit then bill"; per-seat charges compound as your team grows; and many platforms charge separately for related services (image optimization, edge middleware, dedicated compute) that aren\'t shown on the main pricing page. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator pulls overage rates from each provider\'s actual pricing docs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I cap spending so I don\'t get a surprise bill?',
    a: 'Varies by provider, and this is genuinely uneven. AWS has Billing Alerts but no hard cap by default. GCP supports budget caps that can disable billing on a project. Cloudflare and Render have effective spending limits. Vercel, Netlify, and Firebase historically don\'t offer hard caps without enterprise contracts, meaning a viral moment or a bot attack can produce a real five-figure bill. Always set up billing alerts at minimum, ideally before you deploy.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is my usage data uploaded or stored?',
    a: 'No. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator runs entirely in your browser, so the bandwidth, request, storage, and user figures you enter are never uploaded, logged, or stored, and no account is asked for. The comparison is calculated on your device, so your infrastructure plans stay private to you.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How accurate are the estimates?',
    a: 'They are directional, not a final bill. The Best Answer Hub Cloud Cost Calculator uses public list pricing from each provider, which changes over time and excludes commitment discounts such as AWS Savings Plans, up to 72% off, or Google Cloud committed use discounts, up to 70%. Confirm a final figure with the official calculators from AWS, Google Cloud, or Azure before committing.',
  },
];

const seo = {
  title: 'Cloud Cost Calculator — Compare Vercel, AWS & More (2026)',
  description: 'Compare cloud hosting costs across 8 providers. Estimate bandwidth, compute, storage, and per-seat charges before you deploy.',
  url: '/calculators/cloud-cost-calculator/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: '2026-05-23T00:00:00+00:00',
  dateModified: today,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Calculators', url: '/calculators/' },
    { name: 'Cloud Cost Calculator', url: '/calculators/cloud-cost-calculator/' }
  ],
  faq: faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim() })),
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pt-10 pb-6 md:pt-14 md:pb-8">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-5">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/15 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold text-bae-primary">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-bae-primary animate-pulse-dot"></span>
            Updated May 2026 · 8 providers
          </div>
          <a href="/calculators/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink bg-white border border-bae-border px-3.5 py-2 rounded-bae-sm hover:border-bae-primary hover:text-bae-primary transition-colors no-underline shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
            Calculators
          </a>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-bae-ink mb-4">
          Cloud Cost Calculator:<br/>
          <em class="italic text-bae-primary">Compare 8 providers instantly</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-bae-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Pick your frontend host and backend service, enter your expected usage, and see exactly what each provider will cost you. We factored in every free tier, credit, and gotcha.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Calculator Interface -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8" aria-label="Cloud cost calculator">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 xl:grid-cols-[1fr_420px] gap-6 items-start">
        <!-- Left: Inputs -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <!-- Frontend Provider -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 shadow-bae-sm">
            <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-muted mb-4">Frontend Provider</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3" id="frontend-selector">
              <button type="button" data-provider="vercel" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-primary bg-bae-primary-soft ring-1 ring-bae-primary/20">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-primary uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Vercel</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">$20/seat</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">1TB bandwidth</div>
              </button>
              <button type="button" data-provider="netlify" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Netlify</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">$20 flat</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">Credit system</div>
              </button>
              <button type="button" data-provider="cloudflare" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Cloudflare</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">$5 base</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">Free egress</div>
              </button>
              <button type="button" data-provider="amplify" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Amplify</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Pay-as-you-go</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">15GB free</div>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Backend Provider -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 shadow-bae-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
              <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-muted">Backend Provider</h2>
              <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer">
                <input type="checkbox" id="backend-toggle" checked class="w-4 h-4 rounded border-bae-border text-bae-primary focus:ring-bae-primary" />
                <span class="text-sm text-bae-ink font-medium">Include backend</span>
              </label>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3" id="backend-selector">
              <button type="button" data-provider="supabase" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-primary bg-bae-primary-soft ring-1 ring-bae-primary/20">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-primary uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Supabase</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">$25 base</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">250GB egress</div>
              </button>
              <button type="button" data-provider="firebase" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Firebase</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">$0 base</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">PAYG</div>
              </button>
              <button type="button" data-provider="render" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Render</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">$25 + compute</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">Instance-based</div>
              </button>
              <button type="button" data-provider="railway" class="provider-btn text-left px-3 py-3 rounded-bae-sm border border-bae-border bg-white hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Railway</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">$20 min</div>
                <div class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">Per-second</div>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Expected Users -->
          <div class="bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/20 rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 shadow-bae-sm">
            <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-primary mb-4">Expected Users</h2>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-4">
              <div class="flex-1 w-full">
                <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2">Monthly Active Users</label>
                <input type="number" id="expectedUsers" min="0" value="1000" class="w-full text-lg font-semibold border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-4 py-3 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary focus:ring-2 focus:ring-bae-primary/20" />
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">Enter your expected user count and we'll automatically estimate bandwidth, requests, compute, and storage based on typical SaaS usage patterns. Fine-tune individual values below if you know your exact numbers.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Usage Inputs -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 shadow-bae-sm">
            <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-muted mb-5">Expected Monthly Usage</h2>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-5">
              <!-- Bandwidth -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Bandwidth (GB)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-bandwidth">100 GB</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="bandwidth-slider" min="0" max="5000" step="10" value="100" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="bandwidth" min="0" value="100" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Edge Requests -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Edge Requests (millions)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-edgeRequests">1 M</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="edgeRequests-slider" min="0" max="500" step="1" value="1" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="edgeRequests" min="0" value="1" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- API Calls -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">API / Function Calls (millions)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-apiCalls">0.5 M</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="apiCalls-slider" min="0" max="100" step="0.1" value="0.5" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="apiCalls" min="0" step="0.1" value="0.5" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- CPU Hours -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Active CPU Hours</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-activeCpuHours">10 hrs</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="activeCpuHours-slider" min="0" max="500" step="1" value="10" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="activeCpuHours" min="0" value="10" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Storage -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Storage (GB)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-storageGB">50 GB</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="storageGB-slider" min="0" max="1000" step="5" value="50" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="storageGB" min="0" value="50" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Auth MAU -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Auth MAU</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-authMAU">5,000</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="authMAU-slider" min="0" max="500000" step="1000" value="5000" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="authMAU" min="0" value="5000" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- DB Reads -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">DB Reads (100K)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-dbReads">10</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="dbReads-slider" min="0" max="10000" step="10" value="10" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="dbReads" min="0" value="10" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- DB Writes -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">DB Writes (100K)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-dbWrites">5</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="dbWrites-slider" min="0" max="5000" step="5" value="5" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="dbWrites" min="0" value="5" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Build Minutes (Vercel) -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Build Minutes</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-buildMinutes">60 min</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="buildMinutes-slider" min="0" max="5000" step="10" value="60" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="buildMinutes" min="0" value="60" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Production Deploys (Netlify) -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Production Deploys</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-productionDeploys">30</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="productionDeploys-slider" min="0" max="500" step="1" value="30" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="productionDeploys" min="0" value="30" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Vercel Seats -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Team Seats (Vercel)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-seats">1</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="seats-slider" min="1" max="20" step="1" value="1" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="seats" min="1" value="1" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Railway CPU -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Railway vCPU</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-railwayCpu">0.5</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="railwayCpu-slider" min="0.1" max="8" step="0.1" value="0.5" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="railwayCpu" min="0.1" step="0.1" value="0.5" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Railway RAM -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Railway RAM (GB)</label>
                  <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-primary" id="display-railwayRam">0.5</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" id="railwayRam-slider" min="0.1" max="16" step="0.1" value="0.5" class="w-full accent-bae-primary mb-2" />
                <input type="number" id="railwayRam" min="0.1" step="0.1" value="0.5" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Reset -->
          <div class="flex justify-end -mt-1 mb-1">
